## Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes

This resource is the repo's first **"adopt-existing"** resource: schema/
model types are generated by `tfplugingen-framework` from SailPoint's
per-service `/entitlements/v1` OpenAPI spec, and Create/Read/Update/Delete
are hand-written against `golang-sdk/v3`'s
`entitlements.EntitlementsAPIService` client.

- **There is no create or delete endpoint for entitlements.** Entitlements
  only come into existence via source aggregation
  (`POST /entitlements/v1/aggregate/sources/{id}`) and are never deleted
  through this API. `Create` therefore never issues a `POST` - it resolves
  an already-existing entitlement (either directly by `id`, or by looking
  up `source_id` + `value` via a filtered `GET /entitlements/v1` when `id`
  isn't known) and adopts it into Terraform state. `Delete` only removes
  Terraform state (`RemoveResource`) - it never calls the API, and the
  entitlement continues to exist in IdentityNow/ISC afterward.
- **`id` and `value` are Optional+Computed, not Required/Computed-only as
  generated.** The generated schema marked `id` Required (since
  `tfplugingen-openapi` needs *some* attribute as the create-time
  identifier) and `value` Computed-only. This resource hand-overrides both
  so that either `id` alone, or `source_id` + `value` together, can be used
  to adopt an entitlement - matching the reference provider's dual lookup
  modes.
- **Only `requestable`, `segments`, `owner`, `name`, and `description` are
  ever written.** These are the only fields the API's PATCH endpoint
  documents as patchable. Everything else (`attribute`, `value`, `source`,
  `cloud_governed`, `direct_permissions`, `privilege_level`,
  `access_model_metadata`, `tags`, etc.) is aggregated from the source
  system and stays Computed-only - configuring them has no effect.
- **`attributes` and `manually_updated_fields` are hand-added, not
  generated.** Both were declared `additionalProperties: true` in the
  OpenAPI spec, which `tfplugingen-openapi` cannot turn into a usable
  schema. `attributes` (the entitlement's raw, connector-specific source
  attributes) is genuinely dynamic and is exposed as a normalized JSON
  string, the same pattern used by `identitynow_sources_v1`'s
  `connector_attributes`. `manually_updated_fields` is not actually dynamic
  in the underlying SDK type (it has two fixed boolean keys,
  `display_name` and `description`) and is hand-added as a small nested
  Computed object instead of a JSON blob.
- **`access_model_metadata` is Computed-only in this resource.** The reference
  provider manages entries in this list via separate
  `POST`/`DELETE .../access-model-metadata/{attributeKey}/values/{attributeValue}`
  endpoints rather than the entitlement's own PATCH - wiring that up as a
  writable, diffable list is deferred as a follow-up.
- **Updates are computed as a minimal JSON Patch diff** between plan and
  prior state, limited to the writable subset above - only attributes that
  actually changed are included in the `PATCH` request.
